# Machine-managed files: mark as generated so GitHub collapses them in pull
# request diffs and excludes them from language statistics. They are produced by
# bzlmod (MODULE.bazel.lock) and go mod (go.sum) rather than edited by hand.
#
# rules_lint's format multirun (`make format`, `make format-check`, the `format`
# CI job) SKIPS every file whose `linguist-generated`, `gitlab-generated` or
# `rules-lint-ignored` attribute is set — so nothing that is meant to be
# formatted may be marked here. Anchor every pattern with a leading `/` unless
# it really is meant to match at any depth: a bare `BUILD.bazel` matches the
# basename in EVERY directory, and that line once hid all 151 BUILD files
# outside proxy/ from buildifier (#1244).
#
# BUILD / BUILD.bazel are deliberately NOT listed. Gazelle writes the Go rules
# in many of them, but every one also carries hand-written rules, comments,
# `# keep`s and directives that need review, and buildifier formatting is
# idempotent on Gazelle's own output, so `make format` is safe over all of them.
# MODULE.bazel is hand-edited too (like go.mod).
/MODULE.bazel.lock linguist-generated=true
/proxy/MODULE.bazel.lock linguist-generated=true
/go.sum linguist-generated=true
